From c630c52c1615677444b65ae6d7e0200f482341cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:29:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Campus corruption: sieges foul the guild's land; siege
 leftovers finished

- Corruption lives on campus tiles (0-3): tainted drains splinters, blighted
  darkens the doctrine and swaps in the building's blighted form, overrun stops it
- Portal strikes: a foundation beside each nearby building to raze, and blight
  ritualists who channel into the ground (damage breaks the channel)
- A lost strike fouls the Sigil's ground; blight creeps one tile a moon
- Blighted forms: cracked spellglass, tainting Workshop, wild Crucible front,
  leaking Sigil (and loose gates at T3), Grand Hall loses a charter slot
- Cleanse Land and Clear Rubble; destroyed buildings leave rubble
- Undercroft: early word at pattern knowledge 2 (T1), slower learning (T2)
- Marching parties can step home through a T2 Sigil from the Move verb
- Stale castle and posting defense launch markers are cleared on load
- Debug: Foul Campus Ground; round-trip asserts for the new fields

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RF7HNp6pvyXiAz229q52Px
